  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and customers pay for skill and reliability. They judge you by what you can do and how you show up, not by the gap in your record.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is taking one small step every week and logging it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and restarting education after dropping out: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools explain topics, build study plans and practise questions. Passive watching shrinks in value.
  </p>
  <p>
    Consistency, honest planning and proof of skill hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to learn and plan; later, own your routine and your progress.
  </p>

